{"version_id": 61, "article_id": 7, "level_code": "en_a1", "lang": "en", "level": 1, "level_label": "A1 入门", "title": "Germany arrests former spy chief August Hanning", "title_zh": "德国前情报局长汉宁被抓了", "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c58jzyer1kr0o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Helmut_Schmidt%2C_former_German_Chancellor.jpg", "credit": "No machine-readable author provided. Axel Sperl assumed (based on copyright clai · cc0 1.0 · via wikimedia"}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 156, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "A former German spy chief is in trouble with the law. Police arrested him and another man. Both are accused of spying.", "lead_zh": "德国一名前情报局长出事了。警察抓了他和另外一个人，说他们涉嫌间谍活动。", "preview": "August Hanning was the head of Germany's spy service. He led it from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now police", "preview_zh": "奥古斯特·汉宁曾是德国情报机构的负责人。他在1998年到2005年领导这个机构。之后，他做私人顾问。现在警方说他做了坏事。他们说他把秘密情报给了外国。警方没有说这是哪个国家。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 51, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@a79b424/content/audio/7/en_a1.mp3", "duration": 67.338, "size_bytes": 407808, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 182, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@a79b424/content/data/versions/61.json", "paragraphs": ["August Hanning was the head of Germany's spy service. He led it from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now police say he did bad things. They say he spied and gave secret information to a foreign country. Police did not say which country.", "Police also arrested a man named Manfred D. He used to work for the spy service. He stayed there until this year. Police say he gave Hanning about 2,000 secret documents. He did this for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief.", "Police arrested Hanning at his home. His home is in Nordwalde, near Münster. They arrested Manfred D in Bavaria. Hanning must go to court on Wednesday. Manfred D must go to court on Tuesday.", "This is not the first problem for the spy service. In 2023, police charged another spy with treason. They said he gave secrets to Russia. That case is still in court."], "paragraphs_zh": ["奥古斯特·汉宁曾是德国情报机构的负责人。他在1998年到2005年领导这个机构。之后，他做私人顾问。现在警方说他做了坏事。他们说他把秘密情报给了外国。警方没有说这是哪个国家。", "警方还抓了一个叫曼弗雷德·D的人。他以前也在情报机构工作。他一直在那里工作到今年。警方说他给了汉宁大约2000份秘密文件。他这样做是为了钱。曼弗雷德·D是汉宁的办公室主任。", "警方在汉宁家里抓了他。他家在明斯特附近的诺德瓦尔德。他们在巴伐利亚抓了曼弗雷德·D。汉宁周三必须出庭。曼弗雷德·D周二必须出庭。", "这不是这个情报机构第一次出问题。2023年，警方指控另一名间谍犯有叛国罪。他们说他把秘密给了俄罗斯。这个案子还在审理中。"], "body": "August Hanning was the head of Germany's spy service. He led it from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now police say he did bad things. They say he spied and gave secret information to a foreign country. Police did not say which country.\n\nPolice also arrested a man named Manfred D. He used to work for the spy service. He stayed there until this year. Police say he gave Hanning about 2,000 secret documents. He did this for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief.\n\nPolice arrested Hanning at his home. His home is in Nordwalde, near Münster. They arrested Manfred D in Bavaria. Hanning must go to court on Wednesday. Manfred D must go to court on Tuesday.\n\nThis is not the first problem for the spy service. In 2023, police charged another spy with treason. They said he gave secrets to Russia. That case is still in court.", "body_zh": "奥古斯特·汉宁曾是德国情报机构的负责人。他在1998年到2005年领导这个机构。之后，他做私人顾问。现在警方说他做了坏事。他们说他把秘密情报给了外国。警方没有说这是哪个国家。\n\n警方还抓了一个叫曼弗雷德·D的人。他以前也在情报机构工作。他一直在那里工作到今年。警方说他给了汉宁大约2000份秘密文件。他这样做是为了钱。曼弗雷德·D是汉宁的办公室主任。\n\n警方在汉宁家里抓了他。他家在明斯特附近的诺德瓦尔德。他们在巴伐利亚抓了曼弗雷德·D。汉宁周三必须出庭。曼弗雷德·D周二必须出庭。\n\n这不是这个情报机构第一次出问题。2023年，警方指控另一名间谍犯有叛国罪。他们说他把秘密给了俄罗斯。这个案子还在审理中。", "text": "August Hanning was the head of Germany's spy service. He led it from 1998 to 2005. After that, he worked as a private consultant. Now police say he did bad things. They say he spied and gave secret information to a foreign country. Police did not say which country. Police also arrested a man named Manfred D. He used to work for the spy service. He stayed there until this year. Police say he gave Hanning about 2,000 secret documents. He did this for money. Manfred D was Hanning's bureau chief. Police arrested Hanning at his home. His home is in Nordwalde, near Münster. They arrested Manfred D in Bavaria. Hanning must go to court on Wednesday. Manfred D must go to court on Tuesday. This is not the first problem for the spy service. In 2023, police charged another spy with treason. They said he gave secrets to Russia. That case is still in court.", "vocab": [], "title_original": "Former German spy chief arrested for espionage and treason", "summary_original": "August Hanning is accused of obtaining classified information for a foreign power.", "body_original": "Former German spy chief arrested for espionage and treason\nBy\nOlivia Ireland\nPublished\n6 hours ago\nFormer German spy chief August Hanning has been arrested on suspicion of espionage, treason and obtaining classified information for a foreign power, the German Federal Prosecutor's Office says.\nHanning headed the Federal Intelligence Service (BND) from 1998 to 2005 and has since been working as a private consultant.\nProsecutors allege that he used classified intelligence to \"draft an analysis\" for one foreign intelligence service and maintained contact with another foreign spying service. Investigators have not disclosed which foreign powers were involved.\nPolice also arrested former BND employee Manfred D, accusing him of passing Hanning about 2,000 classified documents for money.\nManfred D, who was Hanning's bureau chief and remained in the BND until this year, is charged with aiding and abetting attempted treason and treasonous espionage.\nLocal media reported Hanning was arrested at his home in Nordwalde near Münster while Manfred D was arrested in Bavaria. Hanning is due in court on Wednesday and Manfred D will appear on Tuesday.\nProsecutors say Manfred D, who also served as the chief of staff for Hanning's successors between 2012 and 2026, used his role to gain access to highly confidential information which he then passed on to Hanning \"in exchange for remuneration\".\n\"The current findings suggest that, over the years, Manfred D provided Hanning with approximately 2,000 documents, many of which contained classified information to be used exclusively by the Federal Intelligence Service for internal purposes,\" the statement says.\n\"On one occasion, Hanning used classified intelligence ... to draft an analysis for an officer of a foreign intelligence service,\" prosecutors said, noting it was not clear if \"the material reached the intended recipient\".\nHanning is also accused of being \"in close contact with a representative of another foreign intelligence service, to whom he passed on political information, partially based on material provided by Manfred D, for several years\".\nLocal media say Hanning's alleged possession of intelligence documents came to light during a separate case relating to German steakhouse heiress Christina Block.\nHamburg public prosecutor's office accused Block of orchestrating the kidnapping of her two youngest children in 2023 due to a custody dispute. Investigators allege Hanning was involved in an earlier attempted kidnapping of the children, which he denies.\nState criminal police officers reportedly discovered an electronic data storage device containing sensitive information including recent BND documents.\nIt is not the first time the BND has faced similar controversy. A high-ranking German intelligence officer was\ncharged with treason in 2023\nfor allegedly passing state secrets to Russia.\nProsecutors alleged Carsten L shared intelligence about the war in Ukraine and the Wagner mercenary group and received roughly €400,000 ($450,000; £340,000). His trial is ongoing.\nRelated topics\nGermany\nCorruption\nSpying\nMore on this story\nAlmost 60,000 far-right extremists in Germany, intelligence agency says\nPublished\n30 June\nGermany investigates Russia links to weapons cache discovered in woods, reports say\nPublished\n21 August", "fetched_at": "2026-10-06T16:57:31.470498+00:00", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "August", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.537, "sm": 100, "em": 537, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Hanning", "s": 0.55, "e": 0.9, "sm": 550, "em": 900, "cs": 7, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "was", "s": 0.912, "e": 1.062, "sm": 912, "em": 1062, "cs": 15, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "the", "s": 1.075, "e": 1.162, "sm": 1075, "em": 1162, "cs": 19, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "head", "s": 1.175, "e": 1.425, "sm": 1175, "em": 1425, "cs": 23, "ce": 27, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "of", "s": 1.438, "e": 1.538, "sm": 1437, "em": 1537, "cs": 28, "ce": 30, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "Germany's", "s": 1.55, "e": 2.013, "sm": 1550, "em": 2012, "cs": 31, "ce": 40, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "spy", "s": 2.025, "e": 2.3, "sm": 2025, "em": 2300, "cs": 41, "ce": 44, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "service", "s": 2.312, "e": 2.913, "sm": 2312, "em": 2912, "cs": 45, "ce": 52, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": ".", "s": 2.913, "e": 3.775, "sm": 2912, "em": 3775, "cs": 52, "ce": 53, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "He", "s": 3.775, "e": 3.925, "sm": 3775, "em": 3925, "cs": 54, "ce": 56, "si": 1}, {"i": 11, "w": "led", "s": 3.938, "e": 4.15, "sm": 3937, "em": 4150, "cs": 57, "ce": 60, "si": 1}, {"i": 12, "w": "it", "s": 4.162, "e": 4.275, "sm": 4162, "em": 4274, "cs": 61, "ce": 63, "si": 1}, {"i": 13, "w": "from", "s": 4.287, "e": 4.998, "sm": 4287, "em": 4998, "cs": 64, "ce": 68, "si": 1}, {"i": 14, "w": "1998", "s": 4.998, "e": 5.709, "sm": 4998, "em": 5708, "cs": 69, "ce": 73, "si": 1}, {"i": 15, "w": "to", "s": 5.709, "e": 6.064, "sm": 5708, "em": 6064, "cs": 74, "ce": 76, "si": 1}, {"i": 16, "w": "20